# Generators and the CSV merge driver emit LF bytes. Keep every detected text
# file on that canonical checkout form too, so byte-for-byte verification and
# executable shebangs behave the same under Windows, macOS, and Linux. Binary
# files remain binary because text=auto classifies them before applying eol.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Registry CSVs carry columns a deriver writes, so two branches that each add a
# test or a page collide on numbers neither of them wrote. The merge driver
# named here reads docs/properties.csv to tell a computed cell from an authored
# one, unions the rows on the registry's declared key, and refuses (falling back
# to a normal conflict) on anything it does not fully understand.
#
# Why it matters more than the two minutes it saves: a conflicted pull request
# has no merge ref, so no `pull_request` CI run starts and the head sits at zero
# checks with nothing saying why. See the snag ci-run-silently-not-started
# and derived-field-conflicts-per-branch.
#
# The driver itself is registered per checkout by `npm run setup`; Claude's
# session-githooks.sh delegates to the same implementation. Git config is not
# cloned, so without setup these attributes are inert and a conflict here falls
# back to Git's ordinary behavior.

data/csv-census.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/docs.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/harness.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/kits.csv merge=derived-csv
pages/pages.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/registries.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/tests.csv merge=derived-csv
docs/themes.csv merge=derived-csv
tracker/board-tags.csv merge=derived-csv
tracker/board.csv merge=derived-csv

# An authored registry: the driver unions the rows two branches each add, and
# keeps the row order of whichever branch changed it.
docs/map-tabs.csv merge=derived-csv

# Edit policy: how each file may change. Each value's meaning is a row of
# docs/vocabularies.csv (registry gitattributes, property edit), and
# skills/hooks/check-edit-policy.py holds a commit to it. Later lines win; a
# folder is folder/**, and a negative pattern is not allowed.
*                                     edit=in-place

# Tracker tasks: in place until done, then written once.
tracker/tasks/*.md                    edit=by-status

# The documents docs/docs.csv marks `record`.
docs/github/mcp-server-routing.md     edit=write-once
docs/showing-consolidation.md         edit=write-once
docs/prototypes/md-edit-ideas.json    edit=write-once

# Rebuilt whole by a builder, never by hand: the commit hook's legs
# (node/README.md, "The refresh model") and the page thumbnails.
# linguist-generated folds a file in GitHub's diffs. An index a reviewer reads
# in the diff, such as docs/README.md, stays unfolded. A file with authored
# cells beside computed ones, such as docs/docs.csv, is in place.
dist/web-tools.js                     edit=regenerated linguist-generated
dist/app.js                           edit=regenerated linguist-generated
dist/dictate.js                       edit=regenerated linguist-generated
console/suite.js                      edit=regenerated linguist-generated
pages/index.html                      edit=regenerated linguist-generated
pages/README.md                       edit=regenerated
pages/thumbs/**                       edit=regenerated
docs/README.md                        edit=regenerated
docs/tests.csv                        edit=regenerated linguist-generated
docs/kits.csv                         edit=regenerated linguist-generated
docs/hook-legs.csv                    edit=regenerated linguist-generated
docs/themes.csv                       edit=regenerated linguist-generated
data/csv-census.csv                   edit=regenerated linguist-generated
tracker/board.md                      edit=regenerated
tracker/board.csv                     edit=regenerated linguist-generated
tracker/board-tags.csv                edit=regenerated linguist-generated
skills/default/CONVERSATION.md        edit=regenerated linguist-generated
skills/default/QUALIFIED-WRITING.md   edit=regenerated linguist-generated
plugins/h/skills/**                   edit=regenerated linguist-generated
